@crew fonseca-arjun
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hey. Fonseca, Survey. Lost something? The box on Deck 2 is mine. It's the good one.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. I labelled your locker. Twice. You're welcome.   #funny
- Hi, {me}. Anything lost? Anything found? I'll file it either way.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You're all right, you. Don't spread it about.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Returned three lost things and won at Tiles. Twice.
? mood:low
- Flat day. Someone used the wrong lost-property box. There are four now.
== near
? act:work
- Scanner three's slow. I timed it. I'll be timing it all week.
? deck:3 act:free
- Window shopping. Not buying. Just checking prices for the satisfaction.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The lost-property box has a system. Four colours, two labels. I'll explain it. Sit down.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Pressed flowers. Cruz pretends not to see me pick them. I press them in the chart books.
